# Testing

See `docs/TESTING_GUIDE.md` for the complete guide.

## Stack

- Unit tests: `test` / `flutter_test`
- BLoC tests: `bloc_test` + `mocktail` via `sandBlocTest`
- Fakes/mocks: `packages/testing`

## Coverage Targets

| Layer | Minimum | CI |
|-------|---------|-----|
| `domain/usecases/` | 100% | Blocking |
| `data/` | 80% | Blocking |
| `presentation/bloc/` | 80% | Blocking |
| `presentation/pages/` | 0% | Excluded |

## Rules

- Never mock a concrete class — mock the abstract interface only
- Shared mocks (2+ packages) live in `packages/testing/lib/src/mocks/`
- Every `group` describes the class under test
- Every test name is a behavioural statement in plain English
- No `print()` or `debugPrint()` in test files
- Use `sandBlocTest` / `blocTest` — never `expect(bloc.state, ...)` without the DSL
- Fakes for widget/integration tests; mocks for unit tests

## File Structure

Mirror source: `lib/src/x.dart` → `test/src/x_test.dart`
Golden tests: `test/goldens/` in `design_system` only

## Helpers

```dart
import 'package:testing/testing.dart';

await pumpDsWidget(tester, widget);
final value = await useCase(params).expectRight();
expect(failure, FailureMatchers.isFailureOf<TimeoutFailure>());
```
